# code/gpu31/mmu — MMU model (userspace) + kernel AS-lifecycle helper (patch)

Host model lives in `code/userspace/gpu/panfrost/` (M0 tree, owned by this
slice for `mali_hw.h` / `mali_mmu.h` / `mali_lpae_test.c` / `Makefile`):

- `mali_hw.h` — register map plus the MMU block completed here: FAULTEXTRA
  LO/HI, MMU IRQ pairing (`PAGE_FAULT(n)` / `BUS_ERROR(n)`), TRANSCFG
  identity/mask + AARCH64 PTW fields (named-but-zero on LPAE), LOCK width
  limits, full fault-status field decode (exception byte / access / DEC /
  source ID), LPAE exception classes, AS_ACTIVE poll ceiling.
- `mali_mmu.h` — NEW: freestanding AS lifecycle + invalidate + fault model
  (`mali_as_count/select_ok`, 33-bit VA window + L0 coverage, saturating
  `mali_lock_region`, enable/disable TRANSTAB/MEMATTR values, fault
  class/access/decoder/source/IRQ-pairing/VA decode). Every sequence cites
  kbase r15p0 (LPAE, COHERENCY_NONE) and panfrost v5.2 file:line.
- `mali_lpae_test.c` — 114 M0 checks + 71 new (sections 8–12: AS select,
  33-bit window incl. builder end-to-end, LOCK vectors, AS values, fault
  decode). `make check`: 185 checks, 0 failures, native + qemu-aarch64.
- `Makefile` — test deps gain `mali_mmu.h`.

Kernel helper in this directory:

- `pf7580_as.h` — NEW data-free static-inline header for the 3.10 port:
  `pf7580_as_enable/disable` (TRANSTAB/MEMATTR/TRANSCFG + wmb + UPDATE,
  wait !ACTIVE both sides), `pf7580_as_invalidate` (LOCK + FLUSH_PT/MEM +
  wait), `pf7580_as_wait_ready/write_cmd`, saturating `pf7580_lock_region`,
  IRQ pairing + fault class/access names. No 9630 double-UNLOCK (absent on
  T720 r1p0 errata list). Compiles as a `-c` object against the shared
  3.10.108 tree headers (`CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-`, kbuild
  `modules` stage-2 link OK); module-macro friction seen was gcc-16-vs-3.10
  `cold`-attribute noise in the throwaway harness, not this header.
- `0001-pf7580-as-helper.patch` — adds the header under
  `drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/` (new file only; integrator applies).

Boundary: `G31_Iommu` owns `code/gpu31/iommu/panfrost7580_mmu.*`
(`p7580_mmu_*` / `P7580_*`); this slice uses `mali_*` (host) and
`pf7580_as_*` / `PF7580_*` (kernel). `G31_PanfrostTarget` confirmed no
collision in `code/userspace/gpu/panfrost/`.

## Wiring (integrator)

```sh
patch -p1 < code/gpu31/mmu/0001-pf7580-as-helper.patch
# then #include "pf7580_as.h" from the panfrost port's MMU file and call
# pf7580_as_enable(regs, 0, pgd_dma) after mapping the 0x11400000 window.
```

## Checks run

```sh
cd code/userspace/gpu/panfrost && make check   # 185/185 native + qemu
# kernel header: kbuild M=/tmp/mmuck modules with CROSS_COMPILE=
# aarch64-linux-gnu-, stage-2 link OK (scratch harness, removed)
```
